btract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+5x-2 & =-2+5x \\\\ 3{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-2 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{3}-{x}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of ${x}^{2}.$ We can factor out the ${x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{3}-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(3x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x=0,$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14003" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the real roots of the cubic equation $5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-60x=15x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cab62649-3f2e-56ae-bfd6-8c34dbebf0bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186519582 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(x)=0.$ To do this, we subtract all the terms from the right-hand side so that the right-hand side becomes $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-60x & =15x \\\\ 5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-75x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $5x.$ We can factor out the $5x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-75x & =0 \\\\ 5x({x}^{2}-2x-15) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${x}^{2}-2x-15$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x({x}^{2}-2x-15) & =0 \\\\ 5x(x-5)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=5,$ and $x=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
